\section{Module 2: Multi-Tier Tenant Network Isolation}

\subsection{Objective \& Design Rationale}
Module 2 establishes a dual-tier virtual network architecture to provide logical isolation between public-facing application components and sensitive backend services. By leveraging Neutron Software-Defined Networking (SDN), distinct broadcast domains and granular layer-3 routing policies were configured without physical re-cabling.

\subsection{Implementation Steps}
The network topology was provisioned using the following automated configuration workflow:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{DMZ Network \& Subnet Creation:}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Network Name: \texttt{m2-dmz-net} (\texttt{module2-dmz-net})
        \item Subnet CIDR: \texttt{10.10.10.0/24}, Gateway IP: \texttt{10.10.10.1}, DNS: \texttt{8.8.8.8}
    \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Private Internal Network \& Subnet Creation:}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Network Name: \texttt{m2-private-net} (\texttt{module2-private-net})
        \item Subnet CIDR: \texttt{10.10.20.0/24}, Gateway IP: \texttt{10.10.20.1}, DNS: \texttt{8.8.8.8}
    \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{L3 Router Deployment \& Uplink Gateway Configuration:}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Router Name: \texttt{m2-router} (\texttt{module2-router})
        \item External Gateway: Attached to external provider network \texttt{public} to enable Source Network Address Translation (SNAT) and Floating IP routing.
    \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Subnet Interface Attachment:}
    Attached both \texttt{m2-dmz-subnet} and \texttt{m2-private-subnet} to \texttt{m2-router}, establishing inter-subnet routing capabilities while preserving distinct network boundaries.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Verification \& Topology Analysis}
The provisioned networking components were validated through Horizon and the CLI:

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.88\linewidth]{img/m2-network-list.png}
\caption{Neutron network inventory detailing newly created DMZ and Private subnets.}
\label{fig:m2_networks}
\end{figure}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Subnet Inventory (Figure~\ref{fig:m2_networks}):} Both tenant subnets (\nolinkurl{10.10.10.0/24} and \nolinkurl{10.10.20.0/24}) are registered and active.
    \item \textbf{External Router Gateway (Figure~\ref{fig:m2_router_overview}):} Verified that \texttt{module2-router} possesses an active external gateway interface connected to network \texttt{public}.
    \item \textbf{Router Interfaces (Figure~\ref{fig:m2_router_interfaces}):} Confirmed that \texttt{module2-router} holds two internal active ports serving as default gateways for the DMZ (\texttt{10.10.10.1}) and Private (\texttt{10.10.20.1}) subnets.
\end{itemize}

